{"questions": [{"type": "mcq", "question": "Your child is shown two bar models of the same length. One is shaded to show 1/2 and the other is shaded to show 2/4. Which statement is correct?", "options": ["1/2 is greater than 2/4", "1/2 and 2/4 show the same amount", "2/4 is greater than 1/2", "The two fractions cannot be compared"], "answer": "1/2 and 2/4 show the same amount", "explanation": "When bar models are the same length, you can see that 1/2 (half the bar shaded) covers the same area as 2/4 (two out of four equal parts shaded). These are equivalent fractions.", "tag": "understanding"}, {"type": "short", "question": "Write a fraction equivalent to 1/3 with denominator 6. Draw a bar model to show your answer.", "answer": "2/6", "explanation": "If you cut the bar into 6 equal parts instead of 3, you need to shade twice as many parts. 1/3 = 2/6. Both the numerator and denominator are multiplied by 2.", "tag": "skill_based"}, {"type": "mcq", "question": "Your child looks at two bar models (same length): one shows 3/4 shaded, the other shows 3/8 shaded. Which fraction is larger?", "options": ["3/8 is larger", "3/4 is larger", "They are equal", "Cannot tell from the models"], "answer": "3/4 is larger", "explanation": "When the numerators are the same, the fraction with fewer parts in the whole (smaller denominator) has bigger pieces. 3/4 means 3 big pieces; 3/8 means 3 small pieces.", "tag": "skill_based"}, {"type": "short", "question": "Your child is asked: is 1/2 equivalent to 3/6? Explain your answer using a bar model or by describing the shaded amounts.", "answer": "Yes, 1/2 is equivalent to 3/6. Half the bar (1/2) covers the same amount as 3 out of 6 equal parts (3/6).", "explanation": "Both fractions cover exactly half of the bar model when drawn at the same length. Equivalent fractions name the same amount even though the numbers look different.", "tag": "understanding"}, {"type": "mcq", "question": "Your child needs to find an equivalent fraction for 2/3 with denominator 9. Which is correct?", "options": ["2/9", "3/9", "6/9", "9/9"], "answer": "6/9", "explanation": "The denominator goes from 3 to 9 (multiply by 3). The numerator must also multiply by 3: 2 × 3 = 6. So 2/3 = 6/9.", "tag": "skill_based"}, {"type": "short", "question": "Order these fractions from smallest to largest: 1/4, 1/2, 1/8. You may draw bar models to help.", "answer": "1/8, 1/4, 1/2", "explanation": "When fractions have the same numerator (1), the one with the larger denominator has smaller pieces. Pieces get bigger as the denominator gets smaller, so 1/8 < 1/4 < 1/2.", "tag": "application"}, {"type": "mcq", "question": "Your child sees bar models showing 2/5 and 4/10. Are these equivalent?", "options": ["Yes, they are equivalent", "No, 4/10 is larger", "No, 2/5 is larger", "They cannot be compared"], "answer": "Yes, they are equivalent", "explanation": "To check equivalence, multiply both numerator and denominator of 2/5 by 2: (2 × 2)/(5 × 2) = 4/10. They cover the same shaded area.", "tag": "logical_reasoning"}, {"type": "short", "question": "Your child is given the fraction 3/4 and asked to write it with denominator 8. What fraction should your child write?", "answer": "6/8", "explanation": "To go from denominator 4 to 8, multiply by 2. Multiply the numerator by 2 as well: 3 × 2 = 6. The answer is 6/8.", "tag": "skill_based"}, {"type": "mcq", "question": "Your child looks at two bar models (same length) showing 2/6 and 3/6. Which is greater?", "options": ["2/6 is greater", "3/6 is greater", "They are equal", "Need more information"], "answer": "3/6 is greater", "explanation": "Since both fractions have the same denominator and the bar models are the same length, you just compare the numerators. 3 parts shaded > 2 parts shaded, so 3/6 > 2/6.", "tag": "understanding"}, {"type": "short", "question": "Compare 1/3 and 2/5 using bar models. Which fraction is larger? Explain.", "answer": "2/5 is larger. (Bar model for 1/3 shows the bar cut into 3 parts with 1 shaded; bar model for 2/5 shows the bar cut into 5 parts with 2 shaded. When drawn at the same length, 2/5 covers more area.)", "explanation": "Unlike fractions are easier to compare when you draw both bar models the same length. By looking at the shaded areas, you can see that 2/5 covers more of the bar than 1/3 does.", "tag": "application"}, {"type": "mcq", "question": "Your child must find an equivalent fraction for 5/6 with denominator 12. What is the correct fraction?", "options": ["5/12", "10/12", "7/12", "6/12"], "answer": "10/12", "explanation": "The denominator multiplies by 2 (from 6 to 12). The numerator must also multiply by 2: 5 × 2 = 10. So 5/6 = 10/12.", "tag": "skill_based"}]}
